# llm_note: sent_id 299 — Long complex sentence. "the seats … he did ornament with pure gold" — fronted subj NP with two nested relcl. "he did ornament" = root. "caused a breastwork to be built" = conj of ornament. "that they might rest … upon" = purpose advcl. "upon" is stranded preposition: attach to rest(42). "while they should speak" = advcl of rest(42). "lying and vain words" = obj of speak.
